WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.149
When Marvel hatched their ambitious plan for
a large-scale cinematic universe full of comic-book

00:00:05.149 --> 00:00:08.120
characters, they also kicked off the hottest
new trend in Hollywood.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:14.500
Tinseltown has universe fever, with major
studios all looking to plant a stake in fertile,

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:19.240
franchise-ready territory that they hope someday
will rival the MCU's superheroes for box office

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:19.760
domination.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.840
"...Puny god."

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:26.220
Here are the hottest properties with the potential
to go universal.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:27.800
Call of Duty

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.560
Video game adaptations don't always strike
gold — we're looking at you, Assassin's

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.160
Creed — but the makers of this popular first-person
shooter still believe they can turn their

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.160
prize property into a successful cinematic
universe.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.010
"Okay, game on."

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:46.960
Stacey Sher, a producer known for movies like
Django Unchained and The Hateful Eight, along

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.880
with former Disney executive Nick van Dyk,
are in charge of Activision Blizzard Studios.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.040
They're planning a Call of Duty film franchise
that'll have "the same sort of high-adrenaline,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.540
high-energy aesthetic as the game."

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:03.360
If all goes well, the movies will pay homage
to all the different games in the series,

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.020
from Black Ops to Modern Warfare.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:06.780
Sony Marvel

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.000
"You’re the spiderling.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:11.900
Crime-fighting spider?

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:12.400
You’re Spiderboy?"

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:18.431
Whatever you want to call him, Spider-Man
is back in the MCU fold — but Sony, who

00:01:18.431 --> 00:01:22.520
used to own the web-slinging hero, is still
planning to feature his friends in their own

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:23.810
movie universe.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.300
Venom, starring Tom Hardy in the title role,
will hit theaters in October 2018.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:34.020
Another project, featuring characters Silver
Sable and Black Cat, has a February 2019 release

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:34.540
date.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.740
Just don't expect to see Tom Holland slinging
webs in any of Sony's Marvel films; despite

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.680
some initial confusion, Spidey is an MCU exclusive.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:45.020
"Look kid, there’s a lot going on here that
you don’t understand."

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:46.260
"Stark said you'd say that."

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:47.760
Valiant Comics

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:53.540
Sony's shared superhero universe goes way
beyond Spider-Man's extended family; the studio

00:01:53.549 --> 00:01:58.630
also has a five-picture deal with comics publisher
Valiant, and action-packed movies based on

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:02.080
Bloodshot, Harbinger, and Harbinger Wars are
all in development.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:06.400
Details are sparse, but we do know for sure
that Bloodshot will steer clear of superhero

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:11.180
conventions in favor of a classic sci-fi feel
— and this universe might just have a Guardian

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.360
of the Galaxy in it.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.540
Dave Bautista spilled the beans on Twitter
that he's in talks to headline a film based

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:22.440
on Valiant's Eternal Warrior title, where
he'll be reborn as a whole new kind of hero.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.150
“Ahhh!

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.020
Ha ha ha!

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.000
Yes!”

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:31.740
John Wick

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:37.239
After a pair of successful feature films starring
Keanu Reeves, John Wick is going to explode

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.840
in a whole new direction — with a prequel
TV series.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.940
The small-screen expansion will revolve around
the Continental, the global hotel that caters

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.320
to the world's hottest assassins.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:51.280
But if you love Keanu in the title role, don't
worry; Lionsgate has plans for at least one

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.959
more movie in the John Wick universe, and
considering where we last saw him, this hitman

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.240
has a lot more work to do before he can hang
up his guns.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.120
"Whoever comes.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.240
Whoever it is.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:04.400
I’ll kill them.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.120
I'll kill them all.”

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:08.880
Hasbro

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:10.700
Between the Transformers and G.I.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:16.140
Joe franchises, Hasbro's action figures make
for pretty good action films — and big plans

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:20.480
are in the works for a new Hasbro Universe,
with a team of superhero specialists in charge

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:21.000
of development.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.920
Marvel alums Nicole Perlman, Cheo Coker, and
Joe Robert Cole are all on board, and they're

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.400
ready to reboot G.I.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.640
Joe for a whole new generation.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:33.600
Hasbro's Simon Waters promised that they'll
be blowing up old conventions to create a

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.900
more contemporary Joe, saying,

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.640
"The world has changed, and I think you're
going to see G.I.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:39.620
Joe changing with it."

00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:44.199
So while details are still sparse on Hasbro's
plans for its universe, you know it'll be

00:03:44.199 --> 00:03:45.199
something new.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.460
"And knowing is half the battle!"

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:47.680
The Conjuring

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:52.930
Ed and Lorraine Warren (played by Patrick
Wilson and Vera Farmiga) are a pair of ghost

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:57.109
hunters with a room full of haunted objects
in their house — which turned into a treasure

00:03:57.109 --> 00:04:01.749
trove of movie ideas when Hollywood realized
that the Conjuring franchise was box office

00:04:01.749 --> 00:04:02.260
gold.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:06.800
The demonic haunted doll named Annabelle got
two movies out of the deal, while another

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:10.420
installment featuring the terrifying nun is
due in 2018.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:14.680
And it won't stop there; when it comes to
world of The Conjuring, director James Wan

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:15.920
has ambitious goals:

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:22.820
"One of the biggest things I really wanted
to do is bring respect back to studio horror

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:23.360
films."

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:27.520
With a museum full of haunted objects to choose
from, this is one universe that could keep

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.160
on expanding for a long time.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:30.900
LEGO

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.060
The big bang that spawned this universe came
at the box office, when the LEGO Movie grossed

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.240
four hundred and seventy million dollars worldwide.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:43.169
From there, Warner Brothers dove headfirst
into the world of colorful building blocks,

00:04:43.169 --> 00:04:48.169
with Batman and ninja-themed spin-off movies
as well as a straight sequel called… uh,

00:04:48.169 --> 00:04:49.280
The Lego Movie Sequel.

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:54.839
As for the universe, LEGO Batman Movie director
Chris McKay says it has a "sci-fi premise"

00:04:54.839 --> 00:04:58.620
— in other words, the films are loosely
connected by the fraught relationship between

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.460
the LEGO world and humans who built it.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:04.500
"It's a highly sophisticated interlocking
brick system."

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:05.020
...Whatever.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:08.400
All you need to know that in this universe,
everything is awesome.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:10.140
Hanna-Barbera

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:16.319
It's only a rumor so far, but the buzz surrounding
a full-on movie universe based on classic

00:05:16.319 --> 00:05:20.490
Hanna-Barbera cartoons is definitely building
— starting with a Scooby Doo animated feature

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:21.940
film to be released in 2020.

00:05:22.489 --> 00:05:26.640
If all goes well with Scoob and his gang,
Hollywood can go ahead and bring in a whole

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:32.979
world of classic cartoon characters: The Flintstones,
The Jetsons, Jonny Quest, Top Cat, and of

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:35.500
course, Yogi Bear… whether he likes it or
not.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.260
"Every day it's the same old thing.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:38.460
Look at the bears!

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:38.960
Look at the bears!

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.340
Look at the bears!

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.300
Sheesh."

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:42.980
Millarworld

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:47.020
August 7, 2017 was an important day in the
history of Netflix.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.680
That's when the streaming giant announced
the acquisition of Millarworld— a publishing

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.180
universe that includes plenty of hot Hollywood
properties.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:58.960
Wanted, Kick-Ass, and Kingsman have already
been made into feature films, but they may

00:05:58.979 --> 00:06:03.409
be rebooted on the streaming service, where
Netflix plans to create new original series

00:06:03.409 --> 00:06:07.160
from existing franchises as well as any future
Millarworld titles.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:11.560
Some people even think the Scottish storyteller
might give Marvel's Stan Lee a run for his

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:15.540
money when it comes to creating the most expansive
universe ever seen onscreen.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:17.780
"Excelsior!”

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:19.980
Thanks for watching!

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.320
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:24.860
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

